#---
# purpose: "opaque join of zero-capture function values remains callable through Enum.each/2, which discards the mapper's return"
#---
#
# The mapper is a join of two zero-capture function values, so the each-step
# callsite reaches it through the boxed apply seam rather than a grounded call.
# That seam has one return convention -- the construction wrapper hands a value
# back whatever the caller does with it -- so both halves of the call carry one
# boxed lane and `Enum.each` simply drops it (fz-kdt.155).
def each_a(x), do: dbg(x)
def each_b(x), do: dbg(x)
def run(mapper), do: Enum.each([1, 2, 3], mapper)

def main() do
  mapper = case Process.heap_alloc_stats()[:allocs] == 0 do
    true -> each_a
    _ -> each_b
  end
  run(mapper)
  0
end
